ction that returns True if the object q will fly, and False otherwise.\n    The object q will fly if it's balanced (it is a palindromic list) and the sum of its elements is less than or equal the maximum possible weight w.\n\n    Example:\n    will_it_fly([1, 2], 5) \u279e False \n    # 1+2 is less than the maximum possible weight, but it's unbalanced.\n\n    will_it_fly([3, 2, 3], 1) \u279e False\n    # it's balanced, but 3+2+3 is more than the maximum possible weight.\n\n    will_it_fly([3, 2, 3], 9) \u279e True\n    # 3+2+3 is less than the maximum possible weight, and it's balanced.\n\n    will_it_fly([3], 5) \u279e True\n    # 3 is less than the maximum possible weight, and it's balanced.\n    '''\n\n    def _is_palindromic(q_list):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a list is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        return q_list == q_list[::-1]\n\n    def _sum_elements(q_list):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a list.\"\"\"\n        return sum(q_list)\n\n    is_balanced = _is_palindromic(q)\n    current_weight = _sum_elements(q)\n\n    return is_balanced and (current_weight <= w)", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/77": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "import math\ndef iscube(a):\n    '''\n    Checks if an integer is a perfect cube.\n    Calculates the cube root and verifies if cubing the rounded integer result equals the original number.\n    '''\n    if a == 0:\n        return True\n    \n    cube_root = round(a**(1/3))\n    return cube_root**3 == a", "base_status": "fail", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [[-1]], "plus_fail_tests": [[-8]]}], "HumanEval/65": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "class DigitManipulator:\n    \"\"\"Manages the conversion, counting, and manipulation of digits.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, number: int, shift: int):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the manipulator with the number and shift amount.\"\"\"\n        self._original_number = number\n  